cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DDU-Romania: Dirofilaria Development Unit (DDU) pipeline for Romania, 2005-2024"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AdrianCocian/DDU-Romania"
url: "https://github.com/AdrianCocian/DDU-Romania"
authors:
  - family-names: "Cocian"
    given-names: "Adrian Ionuț"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6329-0793"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, University of Agricultural Sciences and Veterinary Medicine (USAMV) Cluj-Napoca, Romania"
keywords:
  - Dirofilaria
  - Dirofilarial Development Units
  - degree-day model
  - Baskerville-Emin method
  - transmission season
  - ERA5-Land
  - Romania
  - vector-borne disease
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Python pipeline that converts ERA5-Land hourly 2 m air temperature into Dirofilarial
  Development Units (DDU) with four methods (min-max average, hourly average, Baskerville-Emin sine and
  an hourly-sum reference), derives per-grid-cell transmission seasons for Romania (2005-2024; 14 °C
  threshold, 130 DDU or 3120 degree-hours within 30-day rolling windows, 3-day season rule), compares the
  methods and produces the tables and figures of the accompanying manuscript.
